From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:02:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui, sidebar: native subagent surfaces cover ACP
 subagents (RFD children)

Zed a5c4ca8b declared the ACP subagents RFD: an agent announces a child
session (`subagent_update`), the parent registers it, and the child reports
its own activity. Zed's own surfaces for subagents were written for its native
`spawn_agent` tool, and an RFD child fell through three of them. This patch
extends them in place rather than drawing a second set (story 064).

  - Card status. `SubagentStatus` gains `Waiting` for a child that reports
    `RequiresAction`, drawn in the warning colour as "Waiting for you".
    Upstream maps RequiresAction to Running and `can_stop` checks Running;
    both change here, so a waiting child keeps its Stop.
  - Awaiting-permission bar. Besides the tool calls that carry
    `subagent_session_info`, it lists the RFD children whose thread holds a
    pending permission request, and drops one once it is answered. The count
    already included them; `collect_subagent_items_for_sessions` was what
    dropped them.
  - A card without a session message. An announcement creates no transcript
    entry, so a child the parent never wrote to had no card at all. A child
    registered in a turn with no outgoing session message to it by that
    turn's end gets a card after the turn's last entry; a message that arrives
    later replaces it, so there is only ever one. A child named by a tool
    call's `subagent_session_info` is excluded: since upstream #66255 a native
    `spawn_agent` child is registered with an association and has no session
    message either, and without the exclusion it would be drawn twice.
    `unsent_subagents` collects the session ids the thread's tool calls name
    once and filters on them.
  - Sidebar. A thread row reads Background while a subagent is Running or
    Waiting, and waiting-for-answer while one is Waiting, after the permission
    prompt, the question (0030) and an error, which it never hides; a child
    that has not reported, or reports Unknown, is no activity. The row follows
    each child's own StatusChanged, with no event from the parent. Archive is
    refused while a child is active, and the refusal now says why: "This
    thread has running subagents", or, for 0029's background tasks, "This
    thread has running tasks". The rule is one function, `thread_row_status`,
    with 0029/0030's precedence as a truth-table test.

The sidebar half lives here and not in 0029 because it reads 0030's question
state and sits beside 0070's sub-thread markers; this is the last patch of
the claude-agent-acp-plus group, after 0071, so the optional groups after it
(0002, 0052, 0057, 0058, 0063, 0066, 0067) and the test group are generated on
top of it. The row source it reads, `acp_thread::subagent_rows` and
`any_child_active`, is 0034's. Zed's native tool-call children are untouched
apart from the one-card exclusion.

Touch points in upstream files: subagent_card.rs (the status, the unsent
cards), thread_view.rs (the bar and the appended cards), sidebar.rs (the row
status and the archive refusal), and a `watch` dev-dependency for the sidebar
tests. 18 tests added (GPUI integration and unit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
